#38815
spyglass brass north~
a brass spyglass perched on the northern ledge~
A spyglass fashioned in bright brass is fixed on the northern ledge.~
   This long and broad contraption of newfangled brass machinery houses a
serious of polished glass, in an obviously gnomish attempt to further ones
capacities at scanning some distant horizon.  Indeed, it has been securely
fastened to the northern wall, and the swivel bearing mechanism that some
inventor fastened on only allows restricted movement, restraining it to the
northern region.  However, the spyglass hums softly, as if also imbued with
some incantation.  However, that humming can also refer to the obvious lack of
reliability on most gnomish machinery.  Caution would be advised.    
~
